# Rhythmic Central Pattern Generator (CPG)
# Mutual inhibition between extensor and flexor populations generates oscillatory rhythm.

Define a network named cpg_rhythm with timestep 0.003.
# Network with 1 input, 2 LIF neurons, 2 inhibitory linear transforms, 1 output.
# flow: input → extensor ⇄ flexor → output
#        (mutual inhibition creates oscillation)

# Layers:
Define an input port named input with shape (20,).
Define a LIF neuron named extensor with time constant 0.1, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.3.
Define a linear transformation named w_extensor_flexor with weight matrix shape (20, 20).
# inhibitory connection (weights will be negative) — zero-initialised intentionally
Define a LIF neuron named flexor with time constant 0.1, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.3.
Define a linear transformation named w_flexor_extensor with weight matrix shape (20, 20).
# inhibitory connection (weights will be negative) — zero-initialised intentionally
Define an output port named output with shape (20,).

# Connections:
input connects to extensor.
extensor connects to w_extensor_flexor.
w_extensor_flexor connects to flexor.
flexor connects to output.

# recurrent: extensor ↺ flexor
flexor connects to w_flexor_extensor.
w_flexor_extensor connects to extensor.

# Note: firing adaptation (tau=0.5 s) is dropped — not representable in NIR LIF node.
# Future extension: add adaptation current as a separate feedback node.
